```

This reserves stock for each line one by one. If the second reserve fails, the first one has already been deducted. According to spec 7.4: "Stock reservation is all-or-nothing. If any line cannot be reserved, the order is rejected with InventoryError and no stock at all remains reserved for that attempt — including lines that were reserved successfully before the failing one."

The fix: We need to do all reservations atomically. We can either:
1. Try to reserve all without actually modifying stock (peek), then if all succeed, actually reserve.
2. Or reserve and then release on failure.

The simplest approach: try to reserve all; if any fails, release all that were successfully reserved.

